🚀 Snitch V1 — Installation Guide

Install Snitch in seconds using wget.

📥 Quick Install (Recommended)

Run this command in your terminal:

sudo wget -O /usr/local/bin/snitch https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OfficiallyOrbitity/Linux-Extensions/refs/heads/deb/Snitch/Snitch-V1-Core
🔑 Make it Executable
sudo chmod +x /usr/local/bin/snitch
✅ Verify Installation
snitch --help

or try:

sudo snitch python
📦 Requirements

Make sure you have:

bash
wget
systemctl (systemd-based systems)

Install wget if needed:

sudo apt install wget -y
📂 Where it installs
/usr/local/bin/snitch

This means you can run it from anywhere:

sudo snitch <process_name>
❌ Uninstall
sudo rm /usr/local/bin/snitch
⚠️ Notes
Requires sudo for process control
Works with:
Normal processes (python, node, etc.)
System services (auto-detected)
Restart may not work for all processes (depends on how they were launched)
💡 Example Usage
sudo snitch python
sudo snitch nginx
sudo snitch cockpit
